[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3.0,0);
\coordinate (R) at (1.5,2.4);
\draw (P)--(Q);
\draw (Q)--(R);
\draw (R)--(P);
\draw (R) .. controls (0.3,4.0) and (2.7,4.0) .. (R);
\fill (P) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (Q) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (R) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[left] at (R) {$R$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
How many faces does this drawing have?

development.solution_text:
The triangle encloses one region and the loop encloses a second.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3.0,0);
\coordinate (R) at (1.5,2.4);
\draw (P)--(Q);
\draw (Q)--(R);
\draw (R)--(P);
\draw (R) .. controls (0.3,4.0) and (2.7,4.0) .. (R);
\fill (P) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (Q) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (R) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[left] at (R) {$R$};
\node at (1.5,0.8) {$1$};
\node at (1.5,3.2) {$2$};
\node at (3.8,2.6) {$3$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Region $3$ outside the whole drawing is the third face.
$2+1$
$=3$
**The drawing has $3$ faces.**

